                                        "entry_id": "5684f783-0008-3257-9306-61d984384d34",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Able to be sympathized with; meriting sympathy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26b1732f-ce60-4f02-a1bc-0b9a2a1ebe88",
                                                "sense_id": "bf0df33f-9c7c-3aea-9f9b-c5f07f43e388",
                                                "text": "Sympathizable more or less is every person and indeed every animal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e69e9e83-87b8-4b38-883b-d06a871fd484",
                                                "sense_id": "bf0df33f-9c7c-3aea-9f9b-c5f07f43e388",
                                                "text": "But the stakes are higher for McCain as a presidential candidate; what might play as endearingly sympathizable ignorance in your home state becomes more problematic at the national scale, with another 49 state treasuries under your watch."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd4647c9-d7fa-40a5-b012-e442b0505868",
                                                "sense_id": "bf0df33f-9c7c-3aea-9f9b-c5f07f43e388",
                                                "text": "This is in part quite simply because civilizations are conceived as such grand, encompassing entities that it becomes difficult to demonstrate the connections between group belonging and tangible, communicable, sympathizable suffering."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bfe4f6fc-4c4b-42f1-935f-e8f996563f70",
                                                "sense_id": "bf0df33f-9c7c-3aea-9f9b-c5f07f43e388",
                                                "text": "Indeed, his opera Yoake presents itself as a clear example of musical and textual actions unfolding in a linear narrative, whereby characters would appear reasonable, convincing, and (if necessary) sympathizable."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
